insert into kb_chunks (content, source, reference, crop, section, lang, embedding) values ('of mercury bulbs as light traps for egg-laying adults, light trapping of insects should start 5 days before and after the full moon. - Encourage biological control agents, such as small wasps (parasitize the eggs), ground beetles, spiders, crickets, and red ants (attack the eggs, nymphs, and adults), coccinellid beetles, ducks, toads (feed on eggs and nymphs), fungi species (attacks nymphs and adults).

To control black bug infestation:

- During early infestation, raise the water level in the field for 2−3 days to force the insects to move upwards.

